{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-6u:000071:note_appended:bob-cli-6u.1:1c6e34b7f26cb7b9148b7206db81a92dce2b252ff3ff1994eee9a693000963a6","timestamp":"2026-10-12T14:45:22Z","actor":"72","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-6u.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"COORDINATION — docs/task-dependencies.md §12.10 \"Project pull-in\" and §12.11 PP1–PP24 landed in ec7251e (bob-cli-6t.1) just before this phase started. This plan's §12/§13 repair tables do not list them. While rewriting §13, §12.5 and §12.2:\n(a) Keep the §13.4 sentence naming §12.10 as the one close-gesture path that makes ^prj Next.\n(b) Port §12.10's YAML-model wording:\n- Rule step 3 \"N has project reasons (§13.3)\" is vacuous under Design §2, because ^prj reports only its own reasons. Fold it into steps 1–2.\n- PP7: a future project date is now R's own inline [scheduled::], so the result is still_blocked{reason: scheduled}, not reason project.\n- PP8: \"or project depends_on\" becomes R's own Depends-On line.\n- Drop the Gate's \"or N has a non-empty depends_on key\".\n- Drop Trigger (b)'s \"including the derived field for a depends_on property\".\n- PP17's \"legacy internal Depends-On line\": internal ^prj targets are kept on the line but never projected, so R qualifies through trigger (a) only and there is no project_task row to beat.\n(c) §12.10 Writes says \"Nothing else changes\". The recover-rank path (R ? → space; PP10/PP11/PP18 when R was [?]) is an automatic Blocked→Ready recovery, so it writes [unblocked::] per the new freshness §5. The linked ? → * path lands in Next and is skipped.\nIf this is out of scope, record a PROPOSED FOLLOW-UP so 6u.17 picks it up. See research:202610/bob_cli_6t_6u_epic_conflict.md."}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-6u:000072:note_appended:bob-cli-6u.2:8b807b5bcc32784b39e1b2e0a3dad2691940357fac2bd326c9a2e486cbfea673","timestamp":"2026-10-12T14:45:27Z","actor":"72","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-6u.2","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"COORDINATION — bob-cli-6t.2 (project pull-in, running since 10:28 EDT) is editing src/native/projects/scan.rs, mod.rs and edits.rs. It adds a crate-visible drain_state/DrainState that wraps parse_project (open_unhidden_count, unstruck Sub-projects children, the project's future schedule) and makes edits::normalize_task_hide_tag pub(crate). Its reasoning log says it takes §12.10 Rule step 3 from 6s.2's YAML model (project_dependencies::*, frontmatter scheduled/depends_on), because 6s.5 never landed. Before starting, run git log origin/master -- src/native/projects src/native/task_complete. If 6t.2 has landed: revert only the alias helpers from 54a54bf^ (never restore scan.rs wholesale), keep drain_state, and re-point its schedule and project-reason inputs to the ^prj line rather than deleting its callers. See research:202610/bob_cli_6t_6u_epic_conflict.md."}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-6u:000073:note_appended:bob-cli-6u.4:f506165fa037864b2be945ef7051eddceac056f8c8b2718495e9f937f65ec82c","timestamp":"2026-10-12T14:45:33Z","actor":"72","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-6u.4","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"COORDINATION — bob-cli-6t.2 (project pull-in, §12.10) relies on projects::edits::normalize_task_hide_tag (made pub(crate)) for byte-identical #hide removal (PP22). Its PP23 asserts that after a pull-in, bob projects sync --dry-run reports no change for the project. If it has landed, keep that helper's bytes and visibility. Point DrainState's future-schedule input at ^prj's inline date, and keep PP23 passing after the hoist and the Sub-projects reorder (marker after the Depends-On line). The pull-in's SUBOPEN check reads that marker line. See research:202610/bob_cli_6t_6u_epic_conflict.md."}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-6u:000074:note_appended:bob-cli-6u.7:5147507995d2e53e006264e7b547d4d502ee5f3f6f27d3c6c814459e6252bd79","timestamp":"2026-10-12T14:45:38Z","actor":"72","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-6u.7","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"COORDINATION — bob-cli-6t.2 (project pull-in, §12.10, running) adds task_complete/project_pull_in.rs and wires it into plan_successors. The wiring relaxes the [id::] gate and lets a pull-in verdict replace Recover(\"project_task\") for an emptied project's ^prj. It adds trigger/hide_removed to UnblockedRow and StillBlockedRow and a surfaced verb in capture/output.rs. It was planned to build on 6s.5's project verdict, which never landed; this phase now owns that verdict. Whichever lands second must merge, not overwrite:\n(1) StillBlockedProject applies to residents only. ^prj has only its own reasons (Design §2), which §12.10 steps 1–2 already cover.\n(2) The project_member cascade must fire whenever ^prj recovers, including when the pull-in verdict replaced the project_task row. An emptied N can still hold [?] residents tagged #hide, because §12.10's REMAINING skips #hide lines.\n(3) The pull-in's recover-rank path (? → space) writes [unblocked::] through mark_unblocked like every other Ready recovery. The linked ? → * path skips it.\n(4) successors.rs is 1488 lines and both plans say to put new logic in new modules.\nSee research:202610/bob_cli_6t_6u_epic_conflict.md."}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-6u:000075:note_appended:bob-cli-6u.11:69897e58da30c40bc57e6eb991c95a37dd71049ff795345f62811eb16ec7bcfe","timestamp":"2026-10-12T14:45:43Z","actor":"72","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-6u.11","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"COORDINATION — bob-cli-6t.3 (project pull-in plugins phase, running) edits nav 285-unblocked-notice.js: project rows, a \"Project empty\" title, a project_member label, and \"blocked by project\" copy. Its plan bumps the nav manifest \"from the latest master version\" (2.19.0) and deploys nav on this host. A note on 6t.3 asks it to skip 2.20.0 and to leave the deploy until after your salvage. As of 10:45 EDT the deployed ~/bob/.obsidian/plugins/bob-navigation-hotkeys/manifest.json still says 2.20.0. Re-check before you start. If it was replaced, use the newest ~/.local/state/bob-cli/plugin-backups/<ts>/bob-navigation-hotkeys copy whose manifest says 2.20.0. If 6t.3's nav commit landed, rebase on it, merge 285 and the README/package.json rows, and bump from the higher version. See research:202610/bob_cli_6t_6u_epic_conflict.md."}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"bob-cli-6u:000076:note_appended:bob-cli-6u.15:7bfdbc6dea0886693c2c561ac9a94a8f2d9adcc86bb2a2a715279a9ef35d59d0","timestamp":"2026-10-12T14:45:48Z","actor":"72","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"bob-cli-6u.15","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"COORDINATION — bob-cli-6t.3 (running) adds task-status-cycler fragment 088-successor-project.js (projectDrainState, removeProjectHideTags, planProjectPullIns). It edits 085-successor-plan.js (relaxed gate, one row per R, breaker exemption, trigger/hide_removed) and plans a 137-plugin-successor-project.js mixin and 136 receipt changes. It reuses projectDependencyInfo/projectIsBlockedAfter (080) for its step 3. When you move those helpers to the inline ^prj date and the #prj_is_blocked signal, update 6t.3's callers too, and include its recover-rank writes (? → space) in your [unblocked::] rewrite. 085's headroom is shared, so avoid its fragment numbers. See research:202610/bob_cli_6t_6u_epic_conflict.md."}}
